  "id": "DrugBank_DB01331 - MONDO_4264",
  "verbalization": "Cefoxitin, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is implicated in the treatment of bacterial infections through its indication for Escherichia coli infection, Streptococcal infection, and bacterial pneumonia. These conditions are all associated with Cefotetan, a related antibiotic that is indicated for Acute Gonococcal Endometritis. The evidence suggests that Cefoxitin may serve as a bridge in the treatment of this condition, as it is metabolized into Cefotetan, which is directly indicated for Acute Gonococcal Endometritis. The overlapping indications between Cefoxitin and Cefotetan imply a potential mechanism of action where Cefoxitin could contribute to the pathophysiology of the infection, though the exact role remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Cefotetan in the treatment of Acute Gonococcal Endometritis, with Cefoxitin possibly playing a supportive role in the clinical management of the condition.",
